<asp:Content ID="Content3" ContentPlaceHolderID="ContentPlaceHolder2" runat="server">

    <div id="MainBox">
        <h2>
            Frieza is one of the most iconic villains in anime history, rivaling protagonists like Goku <br>
            and Vegeta in both strength and significance. His story spans across, Dragon Ball Z, and Dragon
            Ball Super, and he remains a central figure to the evolution of the series, embodying the essence 
            of villainy, resilience, and pride. Unlike Goku, whose character arcrevolves around growth, 
            goodness, and the pursuit of strength, Frieza's arc focuses on domination,
            revenge, and a terrifying persistence in maintaining his perceived supremacy.
        </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="textBoxes" id="box1">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s history stretches long before his first encounter with the Z Fighters. Born into the <br>
            Cold family, Frieza was raised as royalty, destined to command one of the most powerful forces <br>
            in the universe: his father King Cold’s galactic empire. Unlike many of the characters in <br>
            Dragon Ball Z, Frieza was not a fighter who grew stronger through constant battles; rather, he <br>
            was born with an exceptional natural talent and an overwhelming power level that far exceeded <br>
            most of the known universe. From a young age, Frieza was feared by all, possessing both the <br>
            ruthlessness and intelligence to conquer entire planets effortlessly. His lust for control and <br>
            power knew no bounds, and by the time he reached adulthood, he was regarded as the most feared <br>
            tyrant in the universe.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box2">
        <h2>
            One of Frieza’s greatest achievements was the subjugation of the Saiyan race, whom he saw as <br>
            both tools and potential threats. Recognizing their growing strength and warrior pride, he <br>
            allowed the Saiyans to work under his rule, using them to conquer planets and expand his empire. <br>
            However, he kept a close eye on them, especially after hearing of a legend about a Super Saiyan, a <br>
            warrior of immense power destined to rise among their kind. This legend planted the seed of paranoia <br>
            in Frieza, leading him to ultimately destroy Planet Vegeta and almost all of the Saiyan race.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box3">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s direct involvement in the Dragon Ball Z storyline begins during the Namek Saga. <br>
            However, his influence can be felt much earlier, as his destruction of Planet Vegeta set into <br>
            motion the events that led Goku to Earth. Frieza’s fear of the Saiyans manifested when he ordered <br>
            the annihilation of their planet, effectively eradicating nearly the entire race, sparing only a <br>
            few survivors: Vegeta, Nappa, Raditz, and Goku. He saw the Saiyans as a potential threat to his <br>
            rule, and despite their usefulness, he could not tolerate the possibility of a Super Saiyan <br>
            emerging. Little did Frieza know that his decision to destroy Planet Vegeta would have <br>
            long-lasting consequences, especially concerning Goku.
        </h2>
        <img id="frizaDBZ" src="/images/frizaDBZ.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box4">
        <h2>
            On Namek, Frieza was in search of the Dragon Balls to grant himself immortality, further <br>
            solidifying his reign. His arrival on Namek quickly turned the peaceful planet into a warzone, <br>
            as Frieza began systematically exterminating the Namekians and anyone else who stood in his way. <br>
            His immense power was on full display, as he effortlessly defeated Vegeta and most of the Z <br>
            Fighters, demonstrating his superiority over everyone else.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box5">
        <h2>
            However, Frieza’s overconfidence would soon be his downfall. Goku, who had arrived on Namek <br>
            after a long journey and intense training, stood as Frieza’s greatest obstacle. Their battle <br>
            was monumental, not just for its sheer scale but for what it represented in the series: the <br>
            clash between ultimate good and ultimate evil. Frieza, with his overwhelming power and <br>
            transformations, pushed Goku to his limits. In his final form, Frieza was nearly unstoppable, <br>
            and his cruelty peaked when he killed Krillin, Goku’s best friend. This act of violence <br>
            triggered Goku’s transformation into the legendary Super Saiyan, the very warrior Frieza had <br>
            feared for so long.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box6">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s shock and disbelief at Goku’s transformation were palpable. The tyrant, who had never <br>
            encountered a true challenge, found himself fighting for survival. Despite using 100% of his <br>
            power, Frieza was ultimately no match for Goku’s newfound strength. His arrogance led him to <br>
            his defeat, as he refused to accept Goku’s mercy. After destroying Namek with his own energy <br>
            blast, Frieza was left at Goku’s mercy, but even then, the Saiyan warrior spared his life. <br>
            Frieza, unable to handle the humiliation, attacked Goku from behind, forcing Goku to finally <br>
            end the battle.
        </h2>
        <img id="GokuSjj3" src="/images/GokuSjj3.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box7">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s defeat on Namek marked a turning point in the series. While Goku continued to grow <br>
            stronger and face new threats, Frieza’s story seemed to end—until he was resurrected by his <br>
            father, King Cold, and returned to Earth for revenge. This marked Frieza’s appearance in the <br>
            Trunks Saga, where he was swiftly defeated by Future Trunks, a warrior from the future who had <br>
            surpassed even Goku’s power.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box8">
        <h2>
            This defeat once again solidified Frieza’s fall from grace. However, it would not be the last <br>
            time the galactic tyrant made his mark on the Dragon Ball universe. After spending years in <br>
            Hell, trapped in a cocoon and subjected to endless torment, Frieza returned to prominence in <br>
            Dragon Ball Super.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box9">
        <h2>
            Dragon Ball Super saw the return of Frieza in a major way. After being resurrected by his <br>
            remaining loyal soldiers, Frieza trained for the first time in his life, motivated by a thirst <br>
            for revenge against Goku and Vegeta. His training allowed him to unlock a new form:<span class="form"> Golden <br>
            Frieza</span>, a transformation that significantly increased his power and made him a force to be <br>
            reckoned with once again.
        </h2>
        <img id="Friza3" src="/images/Friza3.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box10">
        <h2>
            The Resurrection F arc showcased Frieza’s growth and persistence. He returned to Earth with a <br>
            massive army, ready to exact revenge on Goku and destroy the Saiyans once and for all. His new <br>
            <span class="form"> Golden form gave him the power to go toe-to-toe with Super Saiyan Blue Goku and Vegeta</span>, but <br>
            once again, Frieza’s arrogance led to his downfall. Unable to maintain his Golden form for <br>
            long due to a lack of stamina, Frieza was ultimately defeated. However, this time, Vegeta—who <br>
            had suffered under Frieza’s rule as a child—delivered the final blow, symbolizing the Saiyans’ <br>
            ultimate victory over their oppressor.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box11">
        <h2>
            Despite his defeat, Frieza’s role in Dragon Ball Super was far from over. He played a key part <br>
            in the Tournament of Power, where Goku recruited him as a last-minute addition to Universe 7’s <br>
            team. Though initially reluctant, Frieza accepted the offer, recognizing the opportunity to <br>
            fulfill his own goals. Throughout the tournament, Frieza proved to be both a valuable ally and <br>
            a cunning adversary, often using his manipulative nature to his advantage. He formed temporary <br>
            alliances with fighters from other universes, only to betray them when it suited him.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box12">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s tactical mind was on full display during the tournament, as he saved Goku multiple <br>
            times and even fought alongside the Saiyan against powerful opponents like Jiren. His willingness <br>
            to work with his enemies, albeit temporarily, showed a different side of Frieza: a side that <br>
            prioritized survival and self-preservation over blind hatred. By the end of the tournament, <br>
            Frieza’s efforts helped secure Universe 7’s victory, and as a reward, Goku revived him, allowing <br>
            him to return to the living world.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box13">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s arc across Dragon Ball Z and Dragon Ball Super is one of the most fascinating character <br>
            developments in the series. Initially introduced as a ruthless tyrant who ruled the universe with <br>
            an iron fist, Frieza’s character evolved into something much more complex. His obsession with power <br>
            and revenge drove him to train and grow stronger, but it also forced him to adapt and evolve as a fighter.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box14">
        <h2>
            While Frieza remains one of the most evil characters in the Dragon Ball universe, his willingness <br>
            to cooperate with Goku and Vegeta in the Tournament of Power demonstrated that he is not a one-dimensional <br>
            villain. He is pragmatic, calculating, and willing to make temporary sacrifices if it means achieving his <br>
            ultimate goal: becoming the ruler of the universe once again.
        </h2>
        <img id="Friza6PosePoint" src="/images/Friza6PosePoint.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box15">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s journey is not one of redemption, as he never seeks to atone for his past actions. Instead,<br> 
            it is a journey of survival and adaptation. He recognizes that the universe has changed since his reign<br> 
            of terror, and in order to regain his place at the top, he must evolve alongside his enemies. His <br>
            willingness to work with Goku and Vegeta, even begrudgingly, shows that Frieza understands the importance <br>
            of power dynamics and the necessity of alliances, even with those he despises.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box16">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s legacy in the Dragon Ball series is undeniable. He is the villain that pushed Goku to <br>
            become a Super Saiyan, the antagonist that forced Vegeta to confront his Saiyan heritage, and the <br>
            tyrant who shaped the history of the universe. His return in Dragon Ball Super and his involvement <br>
            in the Tournament of Power cemented his status as one of the most important characters in the series.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box17">
        <h2>
            Frieza’s influence extends beyond the in-universe narrative. As a villain, he set the standard  <br>
            for future antagonists in Dragon Ball and other shonen anime. His combination of intelligence,  <br>
            cruelty, and overwhelming power made him a memorable and fearsome foe. Even after his defeats, Frieza  <br>
            remained a constant presence in the minds of the characters and fans alike.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box18">
        <h2>
            In conclusion, Frieza’s character arc is one of perseverance, vengeance, and adaptation. <br>
            While he may never seek redemption, his ability to evolve and remain relevant in a universe <br>
            filled with increasingly powerful beings makes him one of the most compelling characters in <br>
            Dragon Ball. Frieza is more than just a villain—he is a force of nature, a symbol of tyranny, <br>
            and a reminder that power, when unchecked, can lead to one’s downfall.
        </h2>
    </div>

